These are consistency models that do not require read/writes to be carved inside blocks
like Weak/Release but there are certain rules:

From Strong to Weak:
<a> Sequential Consistency
    absolutely no local reorderings and writes from separate sources are uniformly
    agreed upon by observers

<b> Total Store Order
    Take SC and allow independent loads to jump past earlier stores from a single
    source. SPARC made this famous.
 
<c> Causal Consistency
    Take TSO and allow stores from separate sources to be seen differently by
    different observers *except* when they are causally related!

<d> Processor Order (FIFO Consistency)
    Only guarantees stores from a single source will not be reordered. Separate
    observers can see different interleavings of stores from separate sources!!

